# mempalace branching policy

All changes in this repository — both local commits and any pushes to GitHub —
land on the `kostadis-dev` branch. Nothing else.

## Rules

- **Commit only on `kostadis-dev`.** Before creating a commit, verify
  `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` is `kostadis-dev`. If it isn't, switch back
  with `git switch kostadis-dev` rather than committing on the wrong branch.
- **Push only `kostadis-dev` to GitHub.** Never push to `main` / `master` /
  any release branch from this repo.
- **Do not create new branches** for features, hotfixes, or experiments
  unless the user explicitly requests one. Stack the work directly on
  `kostadis-dev`.
- **Do not open PRs** against `main` (or any other base) without explicit
  instruction. If the user asks for a PR, default the base to `kostadis-dev`
  and confirm before running `gh pr create`.
- **Never force-push `main` / `master`.** Force-push is allowed on
  `kostadis-dev` only when the user explicitly asks for it.

## When `git status` shows you on the wrong branch

```bash
# ❌ BAD — committing on a feature branch
git checkout -b cursor-harness
git add .
git commit -m "..."

# ✅ GOOD — commit directly on kostadis-dev
git switch kostadis-dev
git add .
git commit -m "..."
```

If you discover you've already committed to the wrong branch, ask the user
how to proceed (cherry-pick, reset, etc.) rather than rewriting history
unprompted.
